    "body": "Will do. Naming is tricky though. Specifically: it might be confusing to claim a document \"has user attention\", when it's the active document's _browser tab_'s visibility and (if not) focus (then focus of its browser window), _NOT_ the visibility and focus of the document itself.\r\n\r\nI.e. the document itself may be invisible and lack focus (e.g. in an iframe), and this property could still be true.\r\n\r\nI'll put something up so we can wordsmith.",
